{"data": [{"author_id": "21293408", "conversation_id": "2120279327589773639", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:55:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120319371809607689"], "id": "2120319371809607689", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@antigravity Shouldn't this just... happen anyway? If we prompt something you need to get it done.", "url": "https://x.com/HarryBarnes/status/2120319371809607689"}, {"author_id": "2806911368", "conversation_id": "2120279327589773639", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:46:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120317217673986061"], "id": "2120317217673986061", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@antigravity The CEO of the scam company blocked me because they were scared of getting busted.    😆 https://t.co/odMEdcmIG7", "url": "https://x.com/Jimmy17999/status/2120317217673986061"}, {"author_id": "2115558973453508609", "conversation_id": "2120279327589773639", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:39:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120315558864502796"], "id": "2120315558864502796", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@antigravity For parallel agents, give the verifier a fresh context with only the spec and the diff. If it sees the builder's reasoning it tends to agree with it. Does the shared message board keep those two views separate?", "url": "https://x.com/ZenoFlow_AI/status/2120315558864502796"}, {"author_id": "1069246220944592901", "conversation_id": "2120279327589773639", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:37:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120314924517998602"], "id": "2120314924517998602", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@antigravity the shared message board is the interesting bit. most multi-agent setups fail at handoff, not at planning. curious how /swarm handles two agents editing the same file?", "url": "https://x.com/GarvSanwariya/status/2120314924517998602"}, {"author_id": "1518878362067865600", "conversation_id": "2120279327589773639", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:34:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120314154015998174"], "id": "2120314154015998174", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@antigravity We need to reset.", "url": "https://x.com/wg5759/status/2120314154015998174"}, {"author_id": "1219767630", "conversation_id": "2120279327589773639", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:34:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120314063083470856"], "id": "2120314063083470856", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@antigravity coordinating agents sounds cool, but it could get chaotic with too many in play", "url": "https://x.com/kimindiehacker/status/2120314063083470856"}, {"author_id": "2806911368", "conversation_id": "2120279327589773639", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:30:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120313204006170756"], "id": "2120313204006170756", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@antigravity @martinmarin", "url": "https://x.com/Jimmy17999/status/2120313204006170756"}, {"author_id": "2806911368", "conversation_id": "2120279327589773639", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:30:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120313108237602956"], "id": "2120313108237602956", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@antigravity The CEO